    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1128">

                <pb facs="1221" n="1209" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg1209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.79658/713: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé to the Norwegian Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-02T19:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 2—6:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Norwegian Series. Foreign Minister Lie<anchor n="30" xml:id="d1128-f1"/>
                    assures me orally (and will confirm by letter) that Norwegian Government desires
                    operation of the American air service described in your 802, February 1, 9 p.m.
                    and states appropriate instructions will be sent immediately to Colonel Berg,
                    Norwegian Military Attaché at Stockholm. He asks me to convey Norwegian
                    Government’s deepest appreciation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1128-f1" n="30" xml:id="d1128-f1-content">
                <p>Trygve Lie, Norwegian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
